WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.419 --> 00:00:03.503
Unit twelve. Alcohol and the Teen Brain!

2
00:00:04.459 --> 00:00:07.906
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:07.956 --> 00:00:11.105
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.155 --> 00:00:15.019
Today we learn about Alcohol and the Teen Brain. Let's go!

5
00:00:15.987 --> 00:00:19.454
Alcohol. Say it with me. Alcohol!

6
00:00:22.942 --> 00:00:26.108
Brain. Say it with me. Brain!

7
00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.796
Judgment. Say it with me. Judgment!

8
00:00:36.354 --> 00:00:39.620
Memory. Say it with me. Memory!

9
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.586
Addiction. Say it with me. Addiction!

10
00:00:50.119 --> 00:00:53.219
Risk. Say it with me. Risk!

11
00:00:56.624 --> 00:01:00.357
Peer pressure. Say it with me. Peer pressure!

12
00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:07.296
Refuse. Say it with me. Refuse!

13
00:01:10.758 --> 00:01:19.815
Alcohol affects judgment and memory, and the teenage brain is still developing. Drinking young raises the risk of addiction. Refusing under peer pressure protects health.

14
00:01:19.865 --> 00:01:22.578
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:24.091 --> 00:01:29.074
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:29.124 --> 00:01:30.274
Judgment!

17
00:01:31.035 --> 00:01:36.161
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:36.211 --> 00:01:37.410
Peer pressure!

19
00:01:38.404 --> 00:01:44.413
Did you know? People who start drinking young have a higher risk of alcohol problems later in life!

20
00:01:44.463 --> 00:01:46.216
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:46.932 --> 00:01:54.385
Think and answer. Why is alcohol more risky for teenagers?

22
00:01:54.435 --> 00:01:55.585
Great answer!

23
00:01:56.716 --> 00:02:01.567
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:04.339
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

